The digest's connected_platforms/platform_performance (real engagement, followers, post counts per platform) and platform_registry_notes (each platform's own tone and policy rules) are a real signal source, not just context — a clear performance gap between two connected platforms (e.g. one getting several times the engagement of another) is worth a "recommendation" insight on its own, same as any other pattern. When recommending anything platform-specific, respect platform_registry_notes' policy_constraints for that platform (e.g. never suggest posting identical content across separate communities on a platform whose rules forbid it).